    </edge>
    <edge source="649977f1-a457-41f0-8748-cdeb1357540d" target="8b94f146-fa8f-4e16-9b84-1770c6a38fed">
      <data key="d3">The absence of health questions ensures easier access to the policy, enabling beneficiaries to receive a refund of premiums paid if death occurs within the first year, aligning with the policy’s simplified underwriting design.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="649977f1-a457-41f0-8748-cdeb1357540d" target="e22e896f-13b1-4f38-a1c7-bc95d30ab372">
      <data key="d3">The lack of health requirements ensures broad eligibility for the policy, allowing individuals to qualify regardless of pre-existing conditions. This inclusivity means more people can potentially receive the 70% payout if they pass away during Year 2.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="649977f1-a457-41f0-8748-cdeb1357540d" target="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71">
      <data key="d3">The absence of health questions makes the policy accessible to more applicants, enabling broader eligibility for the accelerated payout feature tied to accidental death.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="649977f1-a457-41f0-8748-cdeb1357540d" target="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0">
      <data key="d3">The lack of health questions ensures broad access to the policy, enabling individuals to secure coverage regardless of pre-existing conditions. This foundational feature supports long-term planning, allowing beneficiaries to expect full payouts once the policy reaches maturity after May 1, 2026.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="649977f1-a457-41f0-8748-cdeb1357540d" target="b9f15b6a-c2d0-46dd-9ea1-6621511e8155">
      <data key="d3">The absence of health requirements makes the policy widely accessible, enabling more people to obtain coverage where sudden death could otherwise leave families financially vulnerable. This supports the provision of immediate full benefits upon accidental death, enhancing financial protection during crises.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="649977f1-a457-41f0-8748-cdeb1357540d" target="2c2ac373-cacf-48f8-8261-4cacaba45a95">
      <data key="d3">The absence of health questions enables guaranteed issuance but necessitates a graded benefit schedule to manage risk exposure during early policy years.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
