    </edge>
    <edge source="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a" target="fdbea615-6c8b-4e16-b3c0-1e0700ab9386">
      <data key="d3">Knowing that coverage will never decrease reinforces the reliability of the policy’s design, consistent with the characteristics of a simplified issue whole life insurance product.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a" target="95682703-5aa3-4502-9d77-774a9d121b12">
      <data key="d3">Guaranteed unchanging coverage ensures reliable fulfillment of the policy’s primary goal: covering funeral and final expenses.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a" target="592cc5a1-980d-42c3-99cc-7f855ebc5b95">
      <data key="d3">Guaranteed non-decreasing coverage ensures long-term financial security, making the lack of medical requirements even more valuable by simplifying entry into a reliable plan.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a" target="649977f1-a457-41f0-8748-cdeb1357540d">
      <data key="d3">Guaranteed permanent coverage implies consistent benefits, making it unnecessary to ask health-related questions during enrollment.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a" target="8d1da4c9-850a-460c-b431-6c03f074655d">
      <data key="d3">Since coverage will never decrease, it aligns with the commitment that premiums remain fixed, ensuring equitable and sustainable policy performance throughout its duration.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a" target="eb3591d2-1da2-424c-bb9b-68881a3de492">
      <data key="d3">The statement that coverage never decreases ensures that even early claims receive at least some portion of the benefit, such as the 30% payout specified if death occurs in Year 1.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a" target="07cbca12-0349-48ac-8e69-1106566c8841">
      <data key="d3">The policy’s coverage remains constant over time, ensuring consistent protection. This stable coverage applies to the specified face amount of $10,000.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a" target="e22e896f-13b1-4f38-a1c7-bc95d30ab372">
      <data key="d3">The guarantee that coverage never decreases ensures the policy’s benefits grow predictably, supporting the specific 70% payout rule for Year 2 deaths.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a" target="8b94f146-fa8f-4e16-9b84-1770c6a38fed">
      <data key="d3">The statement that coverage never decreases supports the idea that beneficiaries receive at least the amount of premiums paid in Year 1, ensuring minimum protection despite the gradual increase in death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a" target="09323260-bd8d-471c-b093-b779cff6374f">
      <data key="d3">The guarantee that coverage never decreases ensures stable benefit growth, enabling predictable payout conditions like receiving all premiums paid if death happens in Year 2.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a" target="b9f15b6a-c2d0-46dd-9ea1-6621511e8155">
      <data key="d3">The guarantee that coverage never decreases ensures that the full death benefit remains intact, enabling immediate access to it upon accidental death, as stated in the second fact.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a" target="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0">
      <data key="d3">The guarantee that coverage never decreases ensures that once the full benefit becomes available after May 1, 2026, it remains fully accessible. This stability directly enables the condition stated in fact_sentence_2 regarding full payouts post-Year 2.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a" target="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71">
      <data key="d3">The stable nature of coverage ensures that beneficiaries receive the full death benefit when an accident occurs, aligning with the provision that all premiums are included in the payout during such events.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a" target="4ad858e8-94fc-41ca-be39-85f0078c060c">
      <data key="d3">The statement that coverage never decreases ensures the policy maintains its full value over time, supporting the existence of a guaranteed maximum benefit. This stability allows the specified full benefit amount of $10,000 to remain intact throughout the policy term.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a" target="dc80354d-924c-405f-b175-d89bdd4b7c8f">
      <data key="d3">The assertion that coverage will never decrease supports the existence of a graded benefit schedule, where benefits increase progressively over time instead of declining.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a" target="14cae93a-18ec-448c-bb18-ce7724f0cd2e">
      <data key="d3">The guarantee that coverage will never decrease supports the condition stated in fact_sentence_2 that claims can only be denied due to premium non-payment after two years, ensuring policyholder protection beyond initial grading periods.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="72fccced-c720-46a9-8123-caa76992f155" target="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">has stable coverage</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63be0818-6da2-472c-8d0a-f0441f4cce3e" target="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is a stable coverage level of</data>
    </edge>
