    <edge source="eb3591d2-1da2-424c-bb9b-68881a3de492" target="fdbea615-6c8b-4e16-b3c0-1e0700ab9386">
      <data key="d3">The conditional payout of 30% in Year 1 supports the claim that this is a simplified issue whole life policy by illustrating its gradual benefit accumulation feature.</data>
      <data key="d4">examples</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb3591d2-1da2-424c-bb9b-68881a3de492" target="95682703-5aa3-4502-9d77-774a9d121b12">
      <data key="d3">The condition that only 30% of the face amount is paid if death occurs in Year 1 supports the policy’s design to manage risk while still providing partial protection for final expenses.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb3591d2-1da2-424c-bb9b-68881a3de492" target="592cc5a1-980d-42c3-99cc-7f855ebc5b95">
      <data key="d3">A reduced payout in Year 1 reflects an early-stage risk assumption by the insurer, justified by the absence of medical screening, allowing lower initial claims but still ensuring some financial protection.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb3591d2-1da2-424c-bb9b-68881a3de492" target="649977f1-a457-41f0-8748-cdeb1357540d">
      <data key="d3">A lower payout in Year 1 due to the policy's gradual increase aligns with its non-medical underwriting approach, ensuring affordability despite limited early benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">limits</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb3591d2-1da2-424c-bb9b-68881a3de492" target="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a">
      <data key="d3">The 30% payout in Year 1 reflects the minimum guaranteed benefit level, supporting the assertion that coverage never decreases over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">examples</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb3591d2-1da2-424c-bb9b-68881a3de492" target="07cbca12-0349-48ac-8e69-1106566c8841">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 depends on the face amount to determine the actual payout value; it describes how much of the total benefit is paid under specific conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb3591d2-1da2-424c-bb9b-68881a3de492" target="e22e896f-13b1-4f38-a1c7-bc95d30ab372">
      <data key="d3">Death in Year 1 results in a lower payout than if it occurred in Year 2, reflecting a staged increase in benefit availability tied to policy duration.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb3591d2-1da2-424c-bb9b-68881a3de492" target="8b94f146-fa8f-4e16-9b84-1770c6a38fed">
      <data key="d3">When death occurs in Year 1 before May 1, 2025, the payout consists of 30% of the face amount plus a refund of all premiums paid.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb3591d2-1da2-424c-bb9b-68881a3de492" target="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0">
      <data key="d3">Death in Year 1 triggers a limited payout, but if death occurs after Year 2, the full benefit applies due to the policy's escalating terms. This reflects a progressive increase in coverage tied to duration.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb3591d2-1da2-424c-bb9b-68881a3de492" target="4ad858e8-94fc-41ca-be39-85f0078c060c">
      <data key="d3">If death occurs before May 1, 2025, only 30% of the full $10,000 benefit is payable, meaning the payout would be $3,000.</data>
      <data key="d4">derives from</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb3591d2-1da2-424c-bb9b-68881a3de492" target="b9f15b6a-c2d0-46dd-9ea1-6621511e8155">
      <data key="d3">The payout under fact_sentence_1 applies only if death occurs naturally before May 1, 2025; however, if the death is accidental at any point, it triggers the full benefit instead, overriding the reduced rate.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb3591d2-1da2-424c-bb9b-68881a3de492" target="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71">
      <data key="d3">If death happens in Year 1 before May 1, 2025, only 30% of the face amount is paid unless the death was accidental, in which case the full payout—including all premiums—is triggered.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb3591d2-1da2-424c-bb9b-68881a3de492" target="2c2ac373-cacf-48f8-8261-4cacaba45a95">
      <data key="d3">The payout rate specified in fact_sentence_1 is explained by the graded benefit schedule mentioned in fact_sentence_2, which results from the policy's no-exam underwriting approach.</data>
      <data key="d4">justifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
