    <edge source="07cbca12-0349-48ac-8e69-1106566c8841" target="fdbea615-6c8b-4e16-b3c0-1e0700ab9386">
      <data key="d3">The $10,000 face amount defines the core benefit of the simplified issue whole life insurance policy described earlier.</data>
      <data key="d4">specifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07cbca12-0349-48ac-8e69-1106566c8841" target="95682703-5aa3-4502-9d77-774a9d121b12">
      <data key="d3">A $10,000 face amount ensures sufficient financial support to meet the goal of covering funeral and final expenses, aligning with the policy’s intended use.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07cbca12-0349-48ac-8e69-1106566c8841" target="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a">
      <data key="d3">The policy has a fixed face amount of $10,000, which aligns with its promise of unchanging coverage throughout the term.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07cbca12-0349-48ac-8e69-1106566c8841" target="eb3591d2-1da2-424c-bb9b-68881a3de492">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes the baseline monetary value upon which the conditional payouts described in fact_sentence_1 are calculated.</data>
      <data key="d4">used in calculation</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07cbca12-0349-48ac-8e69-1106566c8841" target="e22e896f-13b1-4f38-a1c7-bc95d30ab372">
      <data key="d3">The face amount sets the baseline for calculating payouts; thus, the 70% benefit in Year 2 is derived from this value.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07cbca12-0349-48ac-8e69-1106566c8841" target="8b94f146-fa8f-4e16-9b84-1770c6a38fed">
      <data key="d3">The $10,000 face amount sets the maximum potential benefit, but if death occurs before May 1, 2025, the payout is limited to the total premiums paid rather than the full face value.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07cbca12-0349-48ac-8e69-1106566c8841" target="4ad858e8-94fc-41ca-be39-85f0078c060c">
      <data key="d3">The face amount represents the total death benefit offered by the policy, which aligns exactly with the full benefit amount specified in the second sentence.</data>
      <data key="d4">equals</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">1.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07cbca12-0349-48ac-8e69-1106566c8841" target="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0">
      <data key="d3">The $10,000 face amount serves as the basis for the full payout described in fact_sentence_2, ensuring clarity about what constitutes the "full benefit amount" upon qualifying conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07cbca12-0349-48ac-8e69-1106566c8841" target="b9f15b6a-c2d0-46dd-9ea1-6621511e8155">
      <data key="d3">The $10,000 face amount serves as the basis for the full benefit payable upon accidental death. Fact_sentence_2 depends on this stated amount to determine the exact payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07cbca12-0349-48ac-8e69-1106566c8841" target="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71">
      <data key="d3">The baseline death benefit of $10,000 serves as the foundation for payouts, but in cases of accidental death, the insurer includes all premiums paid, increasing the total benefit above the original face amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
