    <edge source="8b94f146-fa8f-4e16-9b84-1770c6a38fed" target="95682703-5aa3-4502-9d77-774a9d121b12">
      <data key="d3">Since the policy exists to cover funeral and final expenses, an early death within Year 1 triggers a payout equal to the sum of premiums paid, ensuring some financial support despite incomplete benefit accumulation.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8b94f146-fa8f-4e16-9b84-1770c6a38fed" target="649977f1-a457-41f0-8748-cdeb1357540d">
      <data key="d3">The provision allowing full repayment of premiums upon death in Year 1 relies on the policy's streamlined application process, which does not require health disclosures or medical exams.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8b94f146-fa8f-4e16-9b84-1770c6a38fed" target="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a">
      <data key="d3">The rule that premiums paid are returned upon death in Year 1 reinforces the principle that coverage remains stable and does not diminish, even when benefits are limited initially.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8b94f146-fa8f-4e16-9b84-1770c6a38fed" target="eb3591d2-1da2-424c-bb9b-68881a3de492">
      <data key="d3">The inclusion of all premiums paid in the payout during Year 1 complements the base 30% death benefit, forming the complete payout amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8b94f146-fa8f-4e16-9b84-1770c6a38fed" target="07cbca12-0349-48ac-8e69-1106566c8841">
      <data key="d3">The condition that payouts equal premiums paid when death happens in Year 1 depends on the existence of a stated face amount, such as $10,000, which defines the standard benefit level.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
