    <edge source="8b94f146-fa8f-4e16-9b84-1770c6a38fed" target="e22e896f-13b1-4f38-a1c7-bc95d30ab372">
      <data key="d3">Death in Year 1 triggers a refund of all premiums paid, while death in Year 2 results in a partial payout at 70% of the face amount. This reflects a stepwise increase in benefit levels across consecutive years.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8b94f146-fa8f-4e16-9b84-1770c6a38fed" target="09323260-bd8d-471c-b093-b779cff6374f">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines the payout condition for death in Year 1, where beneficiaries receive only the premiums paid. This sets up a baseline before Year 2, when higher benefits become available under different terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8b94f146-fa8f-4e16-9b84-1770c6a38fed" target="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0">
      <data key="d3">Death before May 1, 2025 results in repayment of premiums only, while death on or after May 1, 2026 triggers the full death benefit. This reflects a staged increase in coverage over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8b94f146-fa8f-4e16-9b84-1770c6a38fed" target="4ad858e8-94fc-41ca-be39-85f0078c060c">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines a restricted payout scenario in Year 1, returning only paid premiums, whereas fact_sentence_2 establishes the full death benefit cap at $10,000, providing context for how much could eventually be received.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
