    </edge>
    <edge source="e22e896f-13b1-4f38-a1c7-bc95d30ab372" target="649977f1-a457-41f0-8748-cdeb1357540d">
      <data key="d3">A 70% payout upon death in Year 2 depends on having an active policy under terms set by the insurer. Since no health questions are asked, enrollment remains simple and barrier-free, enabling timely access to such benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e22e896f-13b1-4f38-a1c7-bc95d30ab372" target="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a">
      <data key="d3">The 70% payout condition in Year 2 reflects the progressive nature of the policy's growth, reinforcing that coverage does not diminish over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">examples</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e22e896f-13b1-4f38-a1c7-bc95d30ab372" target="eb3591d2-1da2-424c-bb9b-68881a3de492">
      <data key="d3">The increased payout in Year 2 compared to Year 1 indicates that waiting until later in the policy term leads to greater financial compensation upon death.</data>
      <data key="d4">follows</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e22e896f-13b1-4f38-a1c7-bc95d30ab372" target="07cbca12-0349-48ac-8e69-1106566c8841">
      <data key="d3">The payout percentage in Year 2 relies entirely on the established face amount to compute the actual disbursement.</data>
      <data key="d4">used in calculation</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e22e896f-13b1-4f38-a1c7-bc95d30ab372" target="8b94f146-fa8f-4e16-9b84-1770c6a38fed">
      <data key="d3">A 70% payout applies if death occurs in Year 2, whereas earlier death (Year 1) leads to a higher return equal to total premiums paid. Thus, earlier death yields greater financial recovery relative to later death in the initial period.</data>
      <data key="d4">follows</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e22e896f-13b1-4f38-a1c7-bc95d30ab372" target="09323260-bd8d-471c-b093-b779cff6374f">
      <data key="d3">The first fact defines the death benefit percentage applicable in Year 2, while the second clarifies that all premiums paid are also included in the payout during the same period, adding financial value beyond the base benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e22e896f-13b1-4f38-a1c7-bc95d30ab372" target="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0">
      <data key="d3">Death occurring in Year 2 results in a partial payout, but if death happens after Year 2, specifically on or after May 1, 2026, the full benefit applies due to the policy's maturity schedule.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e22e896f-13b1-4f38-a1c7-bc95d30ab372" target="4ad858e8-94fc-41ca-be39-85f0078c060c">
      <data key="d3">When death occurs in Year 2, the beneficiary receives 70% of the full benefit, which is determined by the $10,000 face amount specified here.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e22e896f-13b1-4f38-a1c7-bc95d30ab372" target="b9f15b6a-c2d0-46dd-9ea1-6621511e8155">
      <data key="d3">The payout percentage in Year 2 depends on non-accidental causes; however, if the cause is accidental, the standard rate does not apply.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e22e896f-13b1-4f38-a1c7-bc95d30ab372" target="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71">
      <data key="d3">The payout rate in Year 2 depends on non-accidental death timing, while accidental death overrides this schedule entirely by including all premiums paid regardless of when it happens.</data>
      <data key="d4">exempted by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e22e896f-13b1-4f38-a1c7-bc95d30ab372" target="ef46c5f5-12c1-4121-869f-787b80ab2ee0">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines the partial payout applicable when death occurs in Year 2 under normal circumstances. This scenario does not apply if the death is classified as accidental, per the definition in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e22e896f-13b1-4f38-a1c7-bc95d30ab372" target="2c2ac373-cacf-48f8-8261-4cacaba45a95">
      <data key="d3">The 70% payout in Year 2 depends on the policy’s graded benefit structure, which exists precisely because no medical underwriting was performed.</data>
