    <edge source="09323260-bd8d-471c-b093-b779cff6374f" target="95682703-5aa3-4502-9d77-774a9d121b12">
      <data key="d3">Since the policy aims to cover funeral and final expenses, receiving all premiums paid in Year 2 strengthens its ability to fulfill that promise financially.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="09323260-bd8d-471c-b093-b779cff6374f" target="8d1da4c9-850a-460c-b431-6c03f074655d">
      <data key="d3">A full refund of all premiums paid at death in Year 2 relies on the continuity of fixed monthly payments, which is ensured by the permanent nature of the premium rate stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="09323260-bd8d-471c-b093-b779cff6374f" target="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a">
      <data key="d3">Receiving all premiums paid upon death in Year 2 relies on the policy's non-decreasing nature, confirming that benefits do not diminish despite early claims.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="09323260-bd8d-471c-b093-b779cff6374f" target="8b94f146-fa8f-4e16-9b84-1770c6a38fed">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 describes the payout rule for death in Year 2, building upon the prior period’s rules by extending eligibility to include more accumulated payments, though still limited to premium recovery at this stage.</data>
      <data key="d4">follows</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="09323260-bd8d-471c-b093-b779cff6374f" target="e22e896f-13b1-4f38-a1c7-bc95d30ab372">
      <data key="d3">The inclusion of all premiums paid in Year 2 complements the 70% death benefit by enhancing total payout, though it does not alter or depend on the benefit’s percentage calculation.</data>
      <data key="d4">adds to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="09323260-bd8d-471c-b093-b779cff6374f" target="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0">
      <data key="d3">Death during Year 2 results in repayment of all premiums paid, while death after Year 2 triggers the full death benefit. This reflects an escalating benefit schedule tied to policy duration.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="09323260-bd8d-471c-b093-b779cff6374f" target="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies that premiums are returned if death occurs in Year 2 due to natural causes. This scenario is subsumed within the broader rule stated in fact_sentence_2, where accidental deaths at any time result in full premium reimbursement.</data>
      <data key="d4">subsumes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="09323260-bd8d-471c-b093-b779cff6374f" target="bc3a5da6-49c7-4acb-96bb-01998b3ff196">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes the payout condition for death in Year 2, including reimbursement of all premiums paid. This depends on the existence of regular payments, which are quantified by fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="09323260-bd8d-471c-b093-b779cff6374f" target="ae8923d1-8746-41d5-842e-11a42617a408">
      <data key="d3">The payout in Year 2 depends on timely premium contributions, which are ensured through automated deductions from the policyholder’s bank account.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="09323260-bd8d-471c-b093-b779cff6374f" target="4ad858e8-94fc-41ca-be39-85f0078c060c">
      <data key="d3">If death occurs in Year 2, the payout consists of all premiums paid up to that point. This amount may contribute toward but does not necessarily equate to the full $10,000 benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">partial payoff</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="09323260-bd8d-471c-b093-b779cff6374f" target="2c2ac373-cacf-48f8-8261-4cacaba45a95">
      <data key="d3">The payout rule in Year 2 depends on the existence of a graded benefit schedule due to the absence of medical underwriting, making the partial benefit applicable before full eligibility.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
