    <edge source="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0" target="fdbea615-6c8b-4e16-b3c0-1e0700ab9386">
      <data key="d3">The rule that full benefits are paid after May 1, 2026, applies specifically to this kind of simplified whole life insurance, reinforcing its structural design and eligibility conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0" target="95682703-5aa3-4502-9d77-774a9d121b12">
      <data key="d3">The full payout eligibility after May 1, 2026, ensures that the policy effectively serves its main purpose of covering funeral and final expenses upon death.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0" target="649977f1-a457-41f0-8748-cdeb1357540d">
      <data key="d3">The condition that full benefits are paid only after May 1, 2026, reflects a built-in waiting period designed to manage risk. This structural requirement complements the policy’s no-medical-exam approach by balancing affordability with controlled exposure.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0" target="8d1da4c9-850a-460c-b431-6c03f074655d">
      <data key="d3">Receiving the full death benefit after Year 2 depends on maintaining active coverage, which relies on consistently paying the unchanged monthly premium.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0" target="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a">
      <data key="d3">Since the full benefit is payable after May 1, 2026, and coverage never decreases, this confirms the permanent nature of the benefit level established from that point onward, supporting the assertion in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0" target="f0521375-da25-4a33-b3ef-2565e3a91ace">
      <data key="d3">The full death benefit is available only after May 1, 2026, ensuring that beneficiaries receive maximum payout upon reaching the maturity threshold. This condition indirectly reflects the policy’s design, including features like incremental benefit growth and cash value accumulation.</data>
      <data key="d4">postdates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0" target="eb3591d2-1da2-424c-bb9b-68881a3de492">
      <data key="d3">The full payout after Year 2 implies that prior periods like Year 1 had lower benefits; thus, the outcome in Year 1 depends on not reaching the later milestone.</data>
      <data key="d4">follows</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0" target="07cbca12-0349-48ac-8e69-1106566c8841">
      <data key="d3">The condition under which the full benefit is paid—the date after May 1, 2026—depends on knowing the actual face amount, making it contingent on the information in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0" target="8b94f146-fa8f-4e16-9b84-1770c6a38fed">
      <data key="d3">The full benefit becomes payable after May 1, 2026, whereas earlier deaths yield only premium refunds. This shows how the payout evolves depending on the timing of death relative to the policy’s maturity date.</data>
      <data key="d4">follows</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0" target="e22e896f-13b1-4f38-a1c7-bc95d30ab372">
      <data key="d3">The full payout becomes effective only after Year 2; thus, any death before that date, such as during Year 2, qualifies for a reduced benefit rather than the maximum.</data>
      <data key="d4">follows</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0" target="09323260-bd8d-471c-b093-b779cff6374f">
      <data key="d3">After Year 2, the full benefit becomes payable, whereas during Year 2, only accumulated premiums are returned. This shows a transition from partial to complete benefit availability.</data>
      <data key="d4">follows</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0" target="4ad858e8-94fc-41ca-be39-85f0078c060c">
      <data key="d3">When death occurs after Year 2 (on or after May 1, 2026), the full death benefit becomes payable. This full amount is explicitly defined as $10,000.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0" target="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines the timeline-based path to full benefits, while fact_sentence_2 introduces an exception based on cause of death, ensuring immediate access to full payouts if death is accidental.</data>
      <data key="d4">exception to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0" target="ef46c5f5-12c1-4121-869f-787b80ab2ee0">
      <data key="d3">The condition for receiving the full death benefit after May 1, 2026, applies generally, except in cases of accidental death, where the full benefit is paid immediately regardless of date.</data>
      <data key="d4">exception to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0" target="bc3a5da6-49c7-4acb-96bb-01998b3ff196">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines when the full death benefit becomes payable, contingent upon surviving past the initial years. This condition depends on maintaining active coverage, which requires consistent payment of the monthly premium stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">requires payment</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0" target="2c2ac373-cacf-48f8-8261-4cacaba45a95">
      <data key="d3">The full payout eligibility after May 1, 2026, results from the graded benefit schedule imposed due to the policy being guaranteed issue without medical screening.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
