    <edge source="4ad858e8-94fc-41ca-be39-85f0078c060c" target="fdbea615-6c8b-4e16-b3c0-1e0700ab9386">
      <data key="d3">The stated full benefit amount of $10,000 depends on the policy being a simplified issue whole life insurance plan, as such policies typically have predefined benefits based on underwriting simplifications.</data>
      <data key="d4">has benefit</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ad858e8-94fc-41ca-be39-85f0078c060c" target="95682703-5aa3-4502-9d77-774a9d121b12">
      <data key="d3">A $10,000 death benefit is established under the policy, specifically intended to cover funeral and final expenses as part of its core function.</data>
      <data key="d4">purpose</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ad858e8-94fc-41ca-be39-85f0078c060c" target="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a">
      <data key="d3">The fixed full benefit of $10,000 reflects the permanent nature of the coverage described in the first sentence, confirming that the benefit remains unchanged and fully accessible when due.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ad858e8-94fc-41ca-be39-85f0078c060c" target="eb3591d2-1da2-424c-bb9b-68881a3de492">
      <data key="d3">The full $10,000 benefit applies when the insured dies after May 1, 2026, or in an accident at any time; it serves as the basis for calculating the reduced 30% payout in Year 1.</data>
      <data key="d4">used in calculation of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ad858e8-94fc-41ca-be39-85f0078c060c" target="07cbca12-0349-48ac-8e69-1106566c8841">
      <data key="d3">The full benefit amount of $10,000 corresponds directly to the policy's established face amount, meaning the entire sum is payable upon qualifying events.</data>
      <data key="d4">equals</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">1.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ad858e8-94fc-41ca-be39-85f0078c060c" target="8b94f146-fa8f-4e16-9b84-1770c6a38fed">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 defines the maximum possible payout of $10,000, which serves as a reference point to understand why fact_sentence_1's mention of returning only paid premiums results in less than the full benefit if death occurs early.</data>
      <data key="d4">sets limit</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ad858e8-94fc-41ca-be39-85f0078c060c" target="e22e896f-13b1-4f38-a1c7-bc95d30ab372">
      <data key="d3">The $10,000 full benefit serves as the base value used to calculate the 70% payout described in the earlier statement for Year 2 claims.</data>
      <data key="d4">used in calculation</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ad858e8-94fc-41ca-be39-85f0078c060c" target="09323260-bd8d-471c-b093-b779cff6374f">
      <data key="d3">The full benefit is set at $10,000, which is only fully payable after May 1, 2026. Therefore, payouts during Year 2 cannot reach this level unless premiums accumulate to exactly $10,000 by then.</data>
      <data key="d4">limits payout</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ad858e8-94fc-41ca-be39-85f0078c060c" target="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0">
      <data key="d3">The full death benefit under the policy is $10,000, which is only accessible if the insured passes away after Year 2, i.e., on or after May 1, 2026.</data>
      <data key="d4">defined by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ad858e8-94fc-41ca-be39-85f0078c060c" target="b9f15b6a-c2d0-46dd-9ea1-6621511e8155">
      <data key="d3">The full benefit of $10,000 becomes immediately accessible upon accidental death, ensuring prompt financial support regardless of policy duration.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ad858e8-94fc-41ca-be39-85f0078c060c" target="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71">
      <data key="d3">The $10,000 death benefit serves as the baseline payout; however, if death occurs accidentally, the beneficiary receives additional compensation equal to all premiums paid, increasing the total payout beyond the standard amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">extends</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ad858e8-94fc-41ca-be39-85f0078c060c" target="b545d862-f828-4173-afa0-6475ca5c91fd">
      <data key="d3">The full death benefit is set at $10,000, but this amount is only payable under specific conditions, including that accidental deaths must occur within 90 days of the incident.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
