      <data key="d3">Accidental death eligibility for full benefits—including all premiums paid—is a key feature enabled by the design of the simplified issue whole life insurance policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71" target="95682703-5aa3-4502-9d77-774a9d121b12">
      <data key="d3">The inclusion of all premiums in the payout for accidental deaths directly supports the policy’s intent to provide comprehensive coverage for funeral and final expenses.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71" target="592cc5a1-980d-42c3-99cc-7f855ebc5b95">
      <data key="d3">The inclusion of all premiums in the accidental death payout enhances the policy’s attractiveness, reinforcing why such policies often waive medical exams—to simplify enrollment while offering strong financial protection.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71" target="649977f1-a457-41f0-8748-cdeb1357540d">
      <data key="d3">The inclusion of all premiums in the payout for accidental death enhances the policy’s appeal, making it especially valuable even for those who might otherwise face barriers due to health issues.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71" target="8d1da4c9-850a-460c-b431-6c03f074655d">
      <data key="d3">The inclusion of all premiums in the accidental death payout relies on consistent contributions, making the stable premium rate essential for maintaining the promised benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71" target="553b7cff-2218-40d7-b664-1ae094b8052a">
      <data key="d3">The inclusion of all premiums in the payout for accidental deaths underscores why coverage does not diminish—it guarantees maximum benefit availability from day one, consistent with permanent protection.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71" target="eb3591d2-1da2-424c-bb9b-68881a3de492">
      <data key="d3">Accidental death at any time results in full payout of premiums and face amount, effectively superseding the reduced payout rule applicable in Year 1.</data>
      <data key="d4">supersedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71" target="07cbca12-0349-48ac-8e69-1106566c8841">
      <data key="d3">Accidental death triggers an enhanced payout that incorporates all previously paid premiums, effectively expanding upon the initial $10,000 face amount established by the policy terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">extends</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71" target="8b94f146-fa8f-4e16-9b84-1770c6a38fed">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 ensures that accidental deaths always include all premiums paid in the payout. This condition overrides the restricted Year 1 rule described in fact_sentence_1, making it more inclusive than the earlier case.</data>
      <data key="d4">exceeds</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71" target="e22e896f-13b1-4f38-a1c7-bc95d30ab372">
      <data key="d3">Accidental death results in full premium reimbursement irrespective of the timeline, making the Year 2 payout rule irrelevant if the death was accidental.</data>
      <data key="d4">overrules</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71" target="09323260-bd8d-471c-b093-b779cff6374f">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes that accidental deaths always trigger full premium repayment, regardless of timing. This includes cases falling into the timeframe described in fact_sentence_1, making it a more inclusive condition than the latter.</data>
      <data key="d4">generalizes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71" target="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies that accidental deaths lead to immediate full payouts, independent of the standard timeline described in fact_sentence_1, where full benefits only activate after May 1, 2026.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies instead of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71" target="4ad858e8-94fc-41ca-be39-85f0078c060c">
      <data key="d3">When an accidental death triggers the full benefit, the original $10,000 death benefit forms the core of the payout, augmented by refunds of all previously paid premiums.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71" target="b9f15b6a-c2d0-46dd-9ea1-6621511e8155">
      <data key="d3">Since all premiums paid are part of the payout, the full benefit is delivered instantly upon accidental death, fulfilling the promise of immediate compensation.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71" target="ef46c5f5-12c1-4121-869f-787b80ab2ee0">
      <data key="d3">The payout rule for accidental death depends on a clear definition of what qualifies as such; without it, the scope of eligibility would be ambiguous.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71" target="b545d862-f828-4173-afa0-6475ca5c91fd">
      <data key="d3">The full payout for accidental death includes all premiums paid, but only if the death occurs within 90 days of the incident. Without this timeframe restriction, the benefit would apply unconditionally.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71" target="ae8923d1-8746-41d5-842e-11a42617a408">
      <data key="d3">The inclusion of all premiums in an accidental death payout relies on regular contributions being made, which are ensured by automated deductions from the policyholder’s bank account.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71" target="2c2ac373-cacf-48f8-8261-4cacaba45a95">
      <data key="d3">The rule that all premiums are paid out upon accidental death depends on the policy's guarantee-issue nature, which necessitates a graded benefit schedule to mitigate risk from adverse selection.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f962e21a-06b9-45a4-a11c-b317bc970f8c" target="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">includes paid premiums in payout for accidental death</data>
    </edge>
