    <edge source="ef46c5f5-12c1-4121-869f-787b80ab2ee0" target="fdbea615-6c8b-4e16-b3c0-1e0700ab9386">
      <data key="d3">Defining "accidental death" supports understanding how the policy delivers immediate benefits, reinforcing why certain conditions override standard waiting periods.</data>
      <data key="d4">supports condition</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ef46c5f5-12c1-4121-869f-787b80ab2ee0" target="95682703-5aa3-4502-9d77-774a9d121b12">
      <data key="d3">Defining accidental death as occurring from a sudden, unexpected injurious event enables the policy’s mechanism to provide timely financial support for funeral and final expenses when such events occur.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ef46c5f5-12c1-4121-869f-787b80ab2ee0" target="e22e896f-13b1-4f38-a1c7-bc95d30ab372">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes the condition for immediate full payout due to accident-related causes. It overrides the tiered payout schedule described in fact_sentence_1, meaning it supersedes the 70% rule for Year 2 deaths.</data>
      <data key="d4">supersedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ef46c5f5-12c1-4121-869f-787b80ab2ee0" target="9b280eb9-7364-4c28-8f15-917ff673f5f0">
      <data key="d3">The definition of accidental death explains why the full benefit may be triggered before May 1, 2026, even though regular payouts require waiting until that date.</data>
      <data key="d4">justifies exception</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ef46c5f5-12c1-4121-869f-787b80ab2ee0" target="b9f15b6a-c2d0-46dd-9ea1-6621511e8155">
      <data key="d3">The rule that the full benefit is paid immediately upon accidental death relies on having a precise definition of "accidental death" to determine eligibility.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ef46c5f5-12c1-4121-869f-787b80ab2ee0" target="52a20188-9d73-4368-9f9f-8eca7f5ffd71">
      <data key="d3">The inclusion of all premiums in the payout upon accidental death relies on having a precise legal definition of accident-related death to ensure consistent application.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ef46c5f5-12c1-4121-869f-787b80ab2ee0" target="b545d862-f828-4173-afa0-6475ca5c91fd">
      <data key="d3">The definition of accidental death requires it to result from a sudden, unexpected injury, but such a claim only qualifies if death occurs within 90 days of the incident.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ef46c5f5-12c1-4121-869f-787b80ab2ee0" target="2c2ac373-cacf-48f8-8261-4cacaba45a95">
      <data key="d3">The definition of accidental death enables immediate full payout despite the graded benefit schedule, making it a critical exception to the delayed benefit rules established due to no-medical-exam underwriting.</data>
      <data key="d4">exception to rule</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
