    <edge source="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae" target="21b0fd78-d6a8-4010-a875-c24ec80a3ec5">
      <data key="d3">Failure to meet the $87.50 monthly payment deadline leads directly to policy cancellation after the grace period ends, underscoring the importance of fulfilling this financial commitment.</data>
      <data key="d4">preceded by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae" target="c010d3b9-4e44-4905-87bb-9b9c8f2843d6">
      <data key="d3">Policy cancellation results from unpaid premiums beyond the grace period, underscoring why a stable, unchanging premium (as stated in fact 1) is essential for maintaining continuous coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">necessitates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae" target="936f48e0-3971-4136-b206-0582810a5f12">
      <data key="d3">Failure to pay by the end of the grace period results in policy cancellation, which stems from an initial unpaid automatic deduction on the 1st of the month.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae" target="456b2a23-de75-4427-a390-d5e6f9113ab0">
      <data key="d3">Policy cancellation follows failure to make a timely payment even after a retry on the 15th, meaning the initial retry was intended to prevent such cancellation.</data>
      <data key="d4">leads to cancellation</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae" target="41063a11-10c3-4717-8757-b3501e3deda2">
      <data key="d3">Failure to make a payment leads to activation of a 30-day grace period, giving the policyholder an opportunity to avoid cancellation. Without timely payment during this period, the policy ceases to remain active.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae" target="81788182-7312-430d-b245-031e37d5c627">
      <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines what happens when payments fail even after the grace period. The second sentence offers a choice in payment frequency that could potentially prevent such failures by reducing transaction risk.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae" target="5896cff7-b1d1-4a7d-97cc-db08bcac9b87">
      <data key="d3">If the policy cancels due to unpaid premiums past the grace period, the original policy document becomes inaccessible, preventing beneficiaries from fulfilling the claim requirement to submit the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae" target="1e415829-df4a-46be-a508-364a4dce0af3">
      <data key="d3">If the policy lapses due to missed payments during the grace period, it cannot support a claim submission. Therefore, maintaining coverage through timely payments enables the beneficiary’s action described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae" target="d3df2cb3-d5f3-464e-bb7d-8d51ca52e9aa">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a certified death certificate hinges on the policy remaining active at the time of death, which depends on whether payment was made during the grace period described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae" target="52aa3801-6bd5-4429-9b25-701f021b5d8a">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a grace period provides temporary protection even if payment fails initially, which is particularly relevant given the policy’s no-medical-question issuance—indicating potentially higher lapse risk among older applicants who might struggle financially.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae" target="dc80354d-924c-405f-b175-d89bdd4b7c8f">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a grace period ensures continued coverage despite late payment, while the graded benefit schedule determines the amount payable upon death based on how long the policy has been active. Together, they shape the timeline-dependent value and stability of the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae" target="ebaa75d8-001d-4086-94ab-307f45c48164">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a 30-day grace period leading to cancellation (fact_sentence_1) is overridden after two years, when the insurer loses the right to cancel—even for missed payments—making the grace period's consequences temporary rather than permanent.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae" target="14cae93a-18ec-448c-bb18-ce7724f0cd2e">
      <data key="d3">The first fact establishes the consequences of missing payments during the grace period, which directly informs the second fact’s assertion that after two years, claims can only be denied due to non-payment—a consistent rule underpinning long-term policy stability.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae" target="7b86f64d-0983-4767-96ea-5e72e39b9a89">
      <data key="d3">The grace period rule applies regardless of misrepresentation history, but after two years, even if there was prior misstatement, the insurer cannot refuse a claim. This ensures claim validity isn’t undermined by early issues once sufficient tenure has passed.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e654e4bf-fd7f-471f-bde4-1f70aaed4e12" target="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is the required payment amount</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e4522d97-9e23-49e0-b1f9-102365cbe2ef" target="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is a potential billing date associated with the payment cycle</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="021df17e-ac00-449d-a7f6-615e56e42360" target="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">may represent a mid cycle reminder or partial deadline</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fe98f628-541d-46aa-bd14-85828da5434f" target="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">defines the length of the grace period</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="62da3b60-b4a7-46c0-8fe4-b6cb1514d4ab" target="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is the timeframe during which payment can be made to prevent policy cancellation</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b1eec2e7-4c7e-4816-8b7e-988cb4a6d97c" target="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">must be paid during grace period</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e99cb29d-935c-4b10-b036-7be8effcc7ff" target="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">amount required to avoid policy cancellation</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7aedafdc-7091-43c6-b62d-643fa6a9c415" target="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">can be used to fund payments to prevent cancellation</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="220375cf-419b-46ef-821c-82ea2d7c7f38" target="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative action to maintain policy status</data>
    </edge>
