      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash values listed in the earlier table reflect the long-term impact of regular premium payments, such as those automatically deducted on the first of each month.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5da67648-ce09-4542-beb6-73a666a8a6f5" target="d20b41a1-58d8-4490-b23e-4806e8417373">
      <data key="d3">The presence of a table detailing guaranteed cash values justifies the assertion that the policy's cash value grows gradually over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">verifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5da67648-ce09-4542-beb6-73a666a8a6f5" target="38b66940-133b-4c2b-b3be-b28ab1f9d404">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value, documented in a prior table, serves as collateral enabling policyholders to borrow funds from the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
