    <edge source="239e4a5a-194e-40ba-8b75-11eb0108b332" target="57d215cb-0353-4d3b-9902-ec5445951305">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states the policy does not exclude war-related deaths, while fact sentence 2 extends this by confirming no aviation-specific exclusion applies either. Together, they emphasize the policy’s inclusive nature regarding dangerous activities.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="239e4a5a-194e-40ba-8b75-11eb0108b332" target="74ba7423-5179-49d9-89b2-ad4c817aeb2b">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states the policy does not exclude war-related deaths, which aligns with the broader theme of minimal restrictions. This supports fact sentence 2’s assertion about no travel restrictions, suggesting comprehensive coverage across risk categories.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="239e4a5a-194e-40ba-8b75-11eb0108b332" target="5d80f781-df38-47eb-959b-57820fc3dcfa">
      <data key="d3">The absence of a war exclusion means the policy covers deaths related to war, which could trigger a claim. This context supports why claiming benefits through designated channels like the toll-free number is relevant.</data>
      <data key="d4">contextual supports</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="239e4a5a-194e-40ba-8b75-11eb0108b332" target="9cd5bddf-be52-46cc-91cf-2bc14462b3ce">
      <data key="d3">The absence of a war exclusion means the policy covers deaths due to war-related causes, which could potentially trigger a claim. This contextual detail supports why submitting proper documentation like a claim form is necessary when such events occur.</data>
      <data key="d4">contextual supports</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="239e4a5a-194e-40ba-8b75-11eb0108b332" target="f0521375-da25-4a33-b3ef-2565e3a91ace">
      <data key="d3">The absence of a war exclusion supports the idea that the policy offers broad protection, consistent with its feature of building substantial cash value over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="239e4a5a-194e-40ba-8b75-11eb0108b332" target="ae6d0ff9-f5aa-4f56-b0e3-b2f05381b7ef">
      <data key="d3">The absence of a war exclusion enhances the policy’s reliability and predictability, especially when paired with its consistently priced $87.50 monthly premium.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="239e4a5a-194e-40ba-8b75-11eb0108b332" target="12aa272e-14b0-400c-bfb5-be55b12c5085">
      <data key="d3">The lack of a war exclusion enhances the reliability of the policy’s broad protection, which complements the stable premium structure outlined in fact_sentence_1. This consistency across financial commitment and coverage inclusivity underscores the policy’s dependability.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="239e4a5a-194e-40ba-8b75-11eb0108b332" target="14c9a49e-b750-4ae4-9750-5cf3f57becb9">
      <data key="d3">The lack of a war exclusion strengthens confidence in the policy's broad protection scope, consistent with the stable, long-term benefits highlighted in chunk summary 1. Furthermore, the mention of auto-draft deductions in chunk summary 2 provides operational clarity for fulfilling the bank draft requirement stated in fact sentence 1.</data>
      <data key="d4">supported by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="239e4a5a-194e-40ba-8b75-11eb0108b332" target="9740e07b-e5dc-49f2-906f-8809e5ba6736">
      <data key="d3">The policy’s inclusion of no war exclusion supports comprehensive coverage, consistent with the beneficiary designation ensuring payout upon death under standard conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">independent support</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="239e4a5a-194e-40ba-8b75-11eb0108b332" target="26f6013f-3536-4d6f-bb66-a0f48884cc23">
      <data key="d3">The absence of a war exclusion in the policy enables Linda Sue Johnson to receive the death benefit even if Dorothy Mae Johnson passed away under circumstances involving war, supporting the validity of her role as beneficiary.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
