    <edge source="d3df2cb3-d5f3-464e-bb7d-8d51ca52e9aa" target="f67c65a1-7ca1-4659-9ab6-9e37f547e284">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate requires prior contact with ComfortCare to ensure proper handling and guidance on submission procedures.</data>
      <data key="d4">follows</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d3df2cb3-d5f3-464e-bb7d-8d51ca52e9aa" target="1e415829-df4a-46be-a508-364a4dce0af3">
      <data key="d3">A certified death certificate verifies the insured's passing, enabling the initiation of the claim process through the submission of a formal claim form.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d3df2cb3-d5f3-464e-bb7d-8d51ca52e9aa" target="b43f297a-8427-44c6-b3de-7251ec721e34">
      <data key="d3">To submit a death certificate, it must be mailed to ComfortCare Claims at the specified address. This ensures proper delivery and processing of the claim documentation.</data>
      <data key="d4">needs address</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d3df2cb3-d5f3-464e-bb7d-8d51ca52e9aa" target="63aa8cb9-583b-4b5a-8fe0-2626eeaf7628">
      <data key="d3">The beneficiary must submit a certified death certificate to trigger the claims process, enabling ComfortCare to evaluate and settle the claim efficiently.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d3df2cb3-d5f3-464e-bb7d-8d51ca52e9aa" target="3b7d9a54-071a-48e0-b6f6-572e65aacf95">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a certified death certificate is a prerequisite step that establishes eligibility for claiming benefits. After providing this evidence, the beneficiary may proceed to submit the policy itself to complete the claim package.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d3df2cb3-d5f3-464e-bb7d-8d51ca52e9aa" target="bbe3a5e7-9762-4606-beaf-78b057d4a71f">
      <data key="d3">A death certificate is required to initiate a claim, but the actual payout amount upon claim approval is determined by the remaining cash value of the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d3df2cb3-d5f3-464e-bb7d-8d51ca52e9aa" target="2c2ac373-cacf-48f8-8261-4cacaba45a95">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a certified death certificate is part of the claim process, but the presence of a graded benefit arises because no medical exam was conducted during application.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d3df2cb3-d5f3-464e-bb7d-8d51ca52e9aa" target="41063a11-10c3-4717-8757-b3501e3deda2">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a certified death certificate initiates the claims process, which relies on the policy remaining active—potentially sustained through the 30-day grace period if needed prior to the insured’s passing.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d3df2cb3-d5f3-464e-bb7d-8d51ca52e9aa" target="12f1e363-6499-41cd-a6c7-5fcd25bfbdae">
      <data key="d3">Failure to make payment during the grace period could result in policy cancellation, potentially preventing the beneficiary from ever needing to submit a death certificate, thus making the instruction in fact_sentence_2 irrelevant in such cases.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d3df2cb3-d5f3-464e-bb7d-8d51ca52e9aa" target="c3965e85-d864-4e4d-835c-0b95792ef2ca">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 details steps for submitting documentation post-death to receive benefits, which complements fact_sentence_1’s mention of cash surrender options, showing that the policy supports multiple forms of value extraction depending on timing and circumstance.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
