    <edge source="e96a90d3-556d-4069-8f21-af575f151db0" target="dc94da25-01fa-41ec-97bf-06bd13328b2f">
      <data key="d3">The 30-day free look period grants the policyholder the right to review the policy and cancel it without penalty. During this window, they may terminate coverage and obtain a complete refund of any payments made.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e96a90d3-556d-4069-8f21-af575f151db0" target="4fa853dd-d204-4e19-ad35-0235ef00f1f0">
      <data key="d3">The 30-day free look period allows policyholders to review their policy without penalty. This period officially begins upon receiving the policy, ensuring timely access to cancellation rights.</data>
      <data key="d4">preceded by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e96a90d3-556d-4069-8f21-af575f151db0" target="6f5e1101-0f4f-4e81-8e61-d356e62a3dc6">
      <data key="d3">The 30-day free look period gives policyholders time to evaluate coverage, especially important since the policy requires no medical underwriting, making early cancellation feasible.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e96a90d3-556d-4069-8f21-af575f151db0" target="3f2c8f57-1f5d-48e3-8f16-209ff8908d42">
      <data key="d3">The 30-day free look period gives the policyholder the right to cancel the policy and receive the cash value before committing long-term. This provision facilitates the act of taking the cash value and terminating coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e96a90d3-556d-4069-8f21-af575f151db0" target="c3965e85-d864-4e4d-835c-0b95792ef2ca">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 mentions a 30-day free look period, providing an early opportunity to terminate coverage, which supports the idea presented in fact sentence 1 that policies can be surrendered for cash value, especially during initial phases when such actions carry no penalties.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e96a90d3-556d-4069-8f21-af575f151db0" target="26f6013f-3536-4d6f-bb66-a0f48884cc23">
      <data key="d3">Dorothy Mae Johnson’s status as a policyholder entitled to a 30-day free look period is relevant because she could choose to modify or terminate the policy before its finalization, thereby affecting whether Linda Sue Johnson remains the intended beneficiary.</data>
      <data key="d4">contextual relationship</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e96a90d3-556d-4069-8f21-af575f151db0" target="4c8ec929-5e52-462b-92a8-e41444e69626">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes a standard consumer protection feature—free look period—that validates and enhances the transparency of the policy described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
