    <edge source="fea6b7a5-3ae3-4bad-b535-981ef6dae0c6" target="f67c65a1-7ca1-4659-9ab6-9e37f547e284">
      <data key="d3">Since beneficiaries can be changed anytime, reaching out to ComfortCare is an acceptable method to initiate such a change.</data>
      <data key="d4">permitted by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fea6b7a5-3ae3-4bad-b535-981ef6dae0c6" target="f416fdfb-665d-40d1-a5b0-42d8b1a53b00">
      <data key="d3">The policy allows unlimited changes to beneficiaries, and one way to do so is by contacting ComfortCare directly. This describes the mechanism through which the stated right is exercised.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fea6b7a5-3ae3-4bad-b535-981ef6dae0c6" target="0cc9a4bc-69ec-4b54-9801-99b95ba12f80">
      <data key="d3">The policyholder has the right to update their beneficiary designation at any time, and this can be done by submitting a formal written request to the insurer.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fea6b7a5-3ae3-4bad-b535-981ef6dae0c6" target="10e87b42-cc43-4448-a557-8ed5882b14c8">
      <data key="d3">The ability to change beneficiaries anytime reflects personal control over policy administration, complementing the broader right to policy portability across state lines.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fea6b7a5-3ae3-4bad-b535-981ef6dae0c6" target="c3965e85-d864-4e4d-835c-0b95792ef2ca">
      <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary does not impact the right to surrender the policy for its cash value, though both highlight the policyholder’s autonomy in managing the policy terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fea6b7a5-3ae3-4bad-b535-981ef6dae0c6" target="5896cff7-b1d1-4a7d-97cc-db08bcac9b87">
      <data key="d3">The right to change beneficiaries anytime supports the integrity of the claims process described in fact_sentence_1 by allowing updates to ensure accurate distribution of benefits upon death.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fea6b7a5-3ae3-4bad-b535-981ef6dae0c6" target="9740e07b-e5dc-49f2-906f-8809e5ba6736">
      <data key="d3">The rule allowing beneficiary changes enables potential updates to the current designation of Linda Sue Johnson, meaning she might not remain the beneficiary indefinitely.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables change</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fea6b7a5-3ae3-4bad-b535-981ef6dae0c6" target="26f6013f-3536-4d6f-bb66-a0f48884cc23">
      <data key="d3">The existing beneficiary designation of Linda Sue Johnson can be modified at any time, meaning her status as beneficiary is not permanent unless maintained through active choice.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables change</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fea6b7a5-3ae3-4bad-b535-981ef6dae0c6" target="3db72c0f-58a3-4898-8687-ac607777538b">
      <data key="d3">The rule permitting policyholders to change beneficiaries applies generally but does not affect the current factual state where Linda Sue Johnson is confirmed as the sole primary beneficiary.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fea6b7a5-3ae3-4bad-b535-981ef6dae0c6" target="4c8ec929-5e52-462b-92a8-e41444e69626">
      <data key="d3">The policy's allowance to change beneficiaries anytime reinforces its flexible nature, supporting potential updates even though the current beneficiary is already designated.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
