    <edge source="f416fdfb-665d-40d1-a5b0-42d8b1a53b00" target="f67c65a1-7ca1-4659-9ab6-9e37f547e284">
      <data key="d3">Changing the beneficiary involves contacting ComfortCare, which aligns with the process described for filing claims, suggesting consistent support procedures.</data>
      <data key="d4">requires contact</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f416fdfb-665d-40d1-a5b0-42d8b1a53b00" target="fea6b7a5-3ae3-4bad-b535-981ef6dae0c6">
      <data key="d3">Contacting ComfortCare enables a policyholder to modify their beneficiary designation, fulfilling the previously mentioned right to make such changes at any time.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains method</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f416fdfb-665d-40d1-a5b0-42d8b1a53b00" target="0cc9a4bc-69ec-4b54-9801-99b95ba12f80">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes calling ComfortCare as a means to change a beneficiary, while fact sentence 2 specifies sending a written request as an alternative method. Both provide different procedural pathways for the same action.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative method</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
