    <edge source="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c" target="b43f297a-8427-44c6-b3de-7251ec721e34">
      <data key="d3">If premium payments halt after two years, the policy remains active through use of cash value, potentially requiring submission of forms by mail to maintain coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">triggers mailout</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c" target="10e87b42-cc43-4448-a557-8ed5882b14c8">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 explains that the policy remains active after two years if premiums stop, relying on accumulated cash value. This ongoing status supports the practical utility of fact sentence 1—the policy being portable—by maintaining enforceable coverage wherever the holder relocates.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c" target="556e501c-b17a-4e61-b49d-34661d54a32a">
      <data key="d3">Automatic continuation upon cessation of premiums preserves coverage over time, complementing the policy’s portability that enables maintenance during relocations.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c" target="23ea9eda-ab01-439d-8c9f-2e04c0f63d59">
      <data key="d3">When premium payments stop after two years, the policy remains active but transitions into a lower-benefit status based on available cash value.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c" target="14c6f6e0-3784-4339-b112-6c08c2eb1083">
      <data key="d3">When premium payments stop after two years, the policy remains active using accumulated cash value. As a result, no further premiums are necessary because the policy operates on its own reserves.</data>
      <data key="d4">implies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c" target="bbe3a5e7-9762-4606-beaf-78b057d4a71f">
      <data key="d3">When premium payments stop after two years, the policy remains active but with diminished benefits. These reduced benefits are calculated according to the existing cash value of the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c" target="3f2c8f57-1f5d-48e3-8f16-209ff8908d42">
      <data key="d3">If premium payments stop after two years, the policy may continue using its cash value. Alternatively, the policyholder has the option to withdraw the cash value and terminate coverage entirely.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c" target="c9e7b542-afe9-4463-8362-f1e619e1c1fa">
      <data key="d3">If premium payments stop after two years, the policy remains active using accumulated cash value. To restore coverage, the policyholder must repay missed premiums with interest, enabling renewal.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c" target="90a0bf93-4726-45a8-be6a-15b19f92a2cc">
      <data key="d3">When premium payments stop after two years, the policy remains active through use of cash value. This ongoing status allows the policyholder to reinstate coverage within two years by restarting payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c" target="2c2ac373-cacf-48f8-8261-4cacaba45a95">
      <data key="d3">The automatic continuation of coverage after two years without premiums is a feature enabled by the policy’s guaranteed-issue nature, though such policies often include restrictions like graded benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c" target="9740e07b-e5dc-49f2-906f-8809e5ba6736">
      <data key="d3">The policy's provision allowing continuation after two years ensures that Linda Sue Johnson retains eligibility to receive the death benefit, reinforcing her designation as the intended recipient.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c" target="26f6013f-3536-4d6f-bb66-a0f48884cc23">
      <data key="d3">The policy’s automatic continuation after two years without premium payment impacts Linda Sue Johnson, as she is named the sole beneficiary entitled to any remaining benefits or cash value.</data>
      <data key="d4">affects beneficiary</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c" target="3db72c0f-58a3-4898-8687-ac607777538b">
      <data key="d3">Since the policy persists via cash value after two years of non-payment, the condition enabling Linda Sue Johnson to collect the full death benefit remains intact over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c" target="4c8ec929-5e52-462b-92a8-e41444e69626">
      <data key="d3">The existence of automatic continuation through cash value use confirms the reliability of the permanent protection offered by the guaranteed issue whole life policy detailed in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c" target="52aa3801-6bd5-4429-9b25-701f021b5d8a">
      <data key="d3">The fact that the policy requires no medical questions justifies its graded benefit structure, explaining why it remains active post-two-year mark despite non-payment risks.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c" target="0f291e01-15ae-4ce0-aed7-ebf20f23c122">
      <data key="d3">The fact that the policy continues automatically after two years if premiums stop is consistent with its guaranteed-issue nature, where no medical exam is required but benefits are initially limited by a graded schedule.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c" target="dc80354d-924c-405f-b175-d89bdd4b7c8f">
      <data key="d3">The automatic continuation of the policy after two years relies on a graded benefit schedule, meaning initial death benefits are restricted and gradually increase, explaining why continued coverage involves reduced benefits when premiums lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e09d524a-e4bc-4ce4-bfc9-16d0d2538a45" target="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">continues automatically after two years if premium payments stop</data>
    </edge>
