    <edge source="23ea9eda-ab01-439d-8c9f-2e04c0f63d59" target="63aa8cb9-583b-4b5a-8fe0-2626eeaf7628">
      <data key="d3">When premiums are not paid after two years, the policy's benefit is reduced, yet ComfortCare still commits to paying valid claims quickly—within five business days—even under diminished coverage terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23ea9eda-ab01-439d-8c9f-2e04c0f63d59" target="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c">
      <data key="d3">The reduction in benefit amount follows directly from the policy's automatic continuation upon cessation of premium payments beyond the initial two-year period.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23ea9eda-ab01-439d-8c9f-2e04c0f63d59" target="bbe3a5e7-9762-4606-beaf-78b057d4a71f">
      <data key="d3">When premiums cease after two years, the policy's benefit is reduced, and this reduced amount is calculated based on the remaining cash value. The cash value serves as the foundation for determining how much coverage remains active.</data>
      <data key="d4">determined by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23ea9eda-ab01-439d-8c9f-2e04c0f63d59" target="14c6f6e0-3784-4339-b112-6c08c2eb1083">
      <data key="d3">When premiums cease after two years, the policy remains active but with lower coverage. This allows the policy to continue indefinitely without requiring any more premium payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23ea9eda-ab01-439d-8c9f-2e04c0f63d59" target="3f2c8f57-1f5d-48e3-8f16-209ff8908d42">
      <data key="d3">When premiums cease after two years, the policy’s benefit reduces unless the policyholder opts to receive the cash value instead. This choice allows termination of coverage while accessing financial value.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23ea9eda-ab01-439d-8c9f-2e04c0f63d59" target="c9e7b542-afe9-4463-8362-f1e619e1c1fa">
      <data key="d3">When premiums lapse after two years, the policy's benefit amount decreases. To restore coverage, the policyholder must repay overdue payments plus interest, allowing renewal of full benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23ea9eda-ab01-439d-8c9f-2e04c0f63d59" target="90a0bf93-4726-45a8-be6a-15b19f92a2cc">
      <data key="d3">When premium payments stop after two years, the policy’s benefit amount decreases unless reinstated. Reinstating the policy within two years allows restoration of original terms before the reduction becomes effective.</data>
      <data key="d4">prevents reduction</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23ea9eda-ab01-439d-8c9f-2e04c0f63d59" target="2c2ac373-cacf-48f8-8261-4cacaba45a95">
      <data key="d3">When premiums cease after two years, the policy's benefit amount decreases due to the application of a graded benefit schedule resulting from the lack of medical underwriting.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23ea9eda-ab01-439d-8c9f-2e04c0f63d59" target="9740e07b-e5dc-49f2-906f-8809e5ba6736">
      <data key="d3">The reduction in benefit amount after two years of non-payment affects the financial outcome for Linda Sue Johnson, who is named as the primary beneficiary, thereby altering the original expectation tied to her designation.</data>
      <data key="d4">impacts beneficiary</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23ea9eda-ab01-439d-8c9f-2e04c0f63d59" target="26f6013f-3536-4d6f-bb66-a0f48884cc23">
      <data key="d3">The policy’s provision that reduces benefits after two years of non-payment affects Linda Sue Johnson, who is designated as the sole primary beneficiary.</data>
      <data key="d4">impacts beneficiary</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23ea9eda-ab01-439d-8c9f-2e04c0f63d59" target="3db72c0f-58a3-4898-8687-ac607777538b">
      <data key="d3">The reduction of the death benefit after two years of non-payment directly affects whether Linda Sue Johnson receives 100%, making her full entitlement dependent on sustained premium payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23ea9eda-ab01-439d-8c9f-2e04c0f63d59" target="4c8ec929-5e52-462b-92a8-e41444e69626">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains that unpaid premiums after two years lead to reduced benefits, which directly applies to the policy detailed in fact_sentence_1, where such reductions would affect the original $10,000 death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">informs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
