    <edge source="14c6f6e0-3784-4339-b112-6c08c2eb1083" target="3b7d9a54-071a-48e0-b6f6-572e65aacf95">
      <data key="d3">Once the policy continues automatically under reduced benefits, the requirement to pay further premiums ceases, making the act of mailing the policy sufficient to trigger this status.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="14c6f6e0-3784-4339-b112-6c08c2eb1083" target="556e501c-b17a-4e61-b49d-34661d54a32a">
      <data key="d3">When premiums stop after two years, the policy continues at reduced benefit levels without requiring additional payments. This feature supports sustained coverage, including during relocations, by maintaining validity across state lines.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="14c6f6e0-3784-4339-b112-6c08c2eb1083" target="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c">
      <data key="d3">The absence of future premium requirements stems from the policy's automatic continuation after two years of non-payment, ensuring ongoing coverage through available cash value.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="14c6f6e0-3784-4339-b112-6c08c2eb1083" target="23ea9eda-ab01-439d-8c9f-2e04c0f63d59">
      <data key="d3">The absence of future premium requirements stems directly from the policy's transition to a reduced-benefit status after two years of non-payment.</data>
      <data key="d4">caused by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="14c6f6e0-3784-4339-b112-6c08c2eb1083" target="bbe3a5e7-9762-4606-beaf-78b057d4a71f">
      <data key="d3">Once the policy continues automatically with reduced benefits, its sustainability hinges entirely on the available cash value, which determines the level of those benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="14c6f6e0-3784-4339-b112-6c08c2eb1083" target="3f2c8f57-1f5d-48e3-8f16-209ff8908d42">
      <data key="d3">If premiums cease and the policy continues under reduced benefit, the policyholder still has the option to terminate it by withdrawing the cash value instead.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="14c6f6e0-3784-4339-b112-6c08c2eb1083" target="90a0bf93-4726-45a8-be6a-15b19f92a2cc">
      <data key="d3">The policy's automatic continuation with reduced benefits allows the policyholder to maintain coverage without paying additional premiums, creating the foundation for potential reinstatement later.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="14c6f6e0-3784-4339-b112-6c08c2eb1083" target="c9e7b542-afe9-4463-8362-f1e619e1c1fa">
      <data key="d3">After two years without premium payments, the policy continues automatically at reduced benefit levels without requiring additional payments. To restore full coverage, the policyholder must repay overdue premiums with added interest.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="14c6f6e0-3784-4339-b112-6c08c2eb1083" target="2c2ac373-cacf-48f8-8261-4cacaba45a95">
      <data key="d3">The policy's automatic continuation without further premiums occurs because it is guaranteed issue, meaning no medical exam was conducted, leading to a graded benefit schedule being applied.</data>
      <data key="d4">caused by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="14c6f6e0-3784-4339-b112-6c08c2eb1083" target="9740e07b-e5dc-49f2-906f-8809e5ba6736">
      <data key="d3">The designation of Linda Sue Johnson as the primary beneficiary becomes subject to modification by the policy’s automatic reduction feature when premiums are no longer paid, which could lower the final payout she receives.</data>
      <data key="d4">impacted by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="14c6f6e0-3784-4339-b112-6c08c2eb1083" target="26f6013f-3536-4d6f-bb66-a0f48884cc23">
      <data key="d3">Since the policy’s automatic continuation with reduced benefits relies on accumulated cash value, the existence of a designated beneficiary like Linda Sue Johnson ensures continuity of the intended inheritance plan despite non-payment.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="14c6f6e0-3784-4339-b112-6c08c2eb1083" target="3db72c0f-58a3-4898-8687-ac607777538b">
      <data key="d3">The condition that no further premiums are needed when the policy continues under reduced benefit undermines the guarantee of receiving 100% of the death benefit, directly affecting the validity of Linda Sue’s entitlement.</data>
      <data key="d4">undermines guarantee</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="14c6f6e0-3784-4339-b112-6c08c2eb1083" target="4c8ec929-5e52-462b-92a8-e41444e69626">
      <data key="d3">Once premiums end after two years, the policy remains active through reduced coverage funded by accumulated cash value, which aligns with the lifelong protection offered by the guaranteed issue whole life policy detailed earlier.</data>
      <data key="d4">complies with</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1aec5cec-23b6-408f-8bf0-4b93d6d60766" target="14c6f6e0-3784-4339-b112-6c08c2eb1083">
