    <edge source="90a0bf93-4726-45a8-be6a-15b19f92a2cc" target="dc94da25-01fa-41ec-97bf-06bd13328b2f">
      <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy within two years after ceasing payments depends on prior eligibility, such as having used the free look period to exit risk-free, allowing a reset of coverage terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="90a0bf93-4726-45a8-be6a-15b19f92a2cc" target="10e87b42-cc43-4448-a557-8ed5882b14c8">
      <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy within two years after ceasing payments preserves its utility, making portability meaningful by allowing transferable coverage even after temporary non-payment.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="90a0bf93-4726-45a8-be6a-15b19f92a2cc" target="556e501c-b17a-4e61-b49d-34661d54a32a">
      <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy within two years after ceasing premium payments allows continued use, including potential relocation without losing coverage. This right complements the policy’s portability feature by maintaining validity during life changes.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="90a0bf93-4726-45a8-be6a-15b19f92a2cc" target="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c">
      <data key="d3">The option to reinstate the policy within two years depends on it remaining active after premium stops, which occurs automatically when payments cease beyond the initial two-year mark.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="90a0bf93-4726-45a8-be6a-15b19f92a2cc" target="23ea9eda-ab01-439d-8c9f-2e04c0f63d59">
      <data key="d3">The option to reinstate the policy within two years serves as a remedy preventing the reduction in benefit amounts that occurs if payments remain suspended past the two-year mark.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables restoration</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="90a0bf93-4726-45a8-be6a-15b19f92a2cc" target="bbe3a5e7-9762-4606-beaf-78b057d4a71f">
      <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy within two years relies on the retained cash value from prior contributions. Since the reduced benefit is calculated using this same cash value, it directly supports the feasibility of renewal.</data>
      <data key="d4">derives from</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="90a0bf93-4726-45a8-be6a-15b19f92a2cc" target="14c6f6e0-3784-4339-b112-6c08c2eb1083">
      <data key="d3">Reinstatement within two years relies on the policy continuing automatically after premium stops, ensuring eligibility even if no new payments are made.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="90a0bf93-4726-45a8-be6a-15b19f92a2cc" target="3f2c8f57-1f5d-48e3-8f16-209ff8908d42">
      <data key="d3">The opportunity to reinstate the policy within two years relies on having access to the accumulated cash value from prior contributions, which becomes available upon cessation of payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="90a0bf93-4726-45a8-be6a-15b19f92a2cc" target="c9e7b542-afe9-4463-8362-f1e619e1c1fa">
      <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate the policy within two years depends on paying back missed premiums plus interest. Without meeting this requirement, reinstatement cannot occur.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional requirement</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="90a0bf93-4726-45a8-be6a-15b19f92a2cc" target="26f6013f-3536-4d6f-bb66-a0f48884cc23">
      <data key="d3">The provision allowing reinstatement within two years applies specifically to Dorothy Mae Johnson’s policy, making it relevant that her daughter Linda Sue Johnson is the designated beneficiary should the policy be revived.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="90a0bf93-4726-45a8-be6a-15b19f92a2cc" target="3db72c0f-58a3-4898-8687-ac607777538b">
      <data key="d3">The option to reinstate the policy within two years supports ongoing coverage, ensuring that the death benefit remains payable to Linda Sue Johnson if the policy is revived before expiration.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="90a0bf93-4726-45a8-be6a-15b19f92a2cc" target="4c8ec929-5e52-462b-92a8-e41444e69626">
      <data key="d3">The provision allowing reinstatement within two years supports the viability of the guaranteed issue whole life policy by ensuring coverage can resume even after missed payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
