    <edge source="c9e7b542-afe9-4463-8362-f1e619e1c1fa" target="3b7d9a54-071a-48e0-b6f6-572e65aacf95">
      <data key="d3">Paying missed premiums with interest allows the policyholder to restore coverage, making the act of mailing the policy relevant to initiating such recovery efforts.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c9e7b542-afe9-4463-8362-f1e619e1c1fa" target="b43f297a-8427-44c6-b3de-7251ec721e34">
      <data key="d3">Reinstating a policy involves remitting past-due premiums with interest, which would typically require sending funds to the designated claims mailing address.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c9e7b542-afe9-4463-8362-f1e619e1c1fa" target="dc94da25-01fa-41ec-97bf-06bd13328b2f">
      <data key="d3">Reinstating a canceled policy requires repaying missed premiums with interest, which only applies if the policy was previously terminated—even briefly—during the free look window.</data>
      <data key="d4">necessary for recovery</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c9e7b542-afe9-4463-8362-f1e619e1c1fa" target="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to pay missed premiums with interest applies only because the policy continues automatically after two years without payment, ensuring eligibility for reinstatement.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c9e7b542-afe9-4463-8362-f1e619e1c1fa" target="23ea9eda-ab01-439d-8c9f-2e04c0f63d59">
      <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy requires repaying missed premiums with interest, which reverses the effect of reduced benefits caused by non-payment beyond two years.</data>
      <data key="d4">reverses</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c9e7b542-afe9-4463-8362-f1e619e1c1fa" target="bbe3a5e7-9762-4606-beaf-78b057d4a71f">
      <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy requires paying overdue premiums with interest, which directly affects the available cash value used to calculate the reduced benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c9e7b542-afe9-4463-8362-f1e619e1c1fa" target="14c6f6e0-3784-4339-b112-6c08c2eb1083">
      <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy involves paying back missed premiums plus interest, which allows restoration of full benefits. This action follows the initial state where the policy has already continued automatically under reduced benefits due to non-payment.</data>
      <data key="d4">follows</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c9e7b542-afe9-4463-8362-f1e619e1c1fa" target="3f2c8f57-1f5d-48e3-8f16-209ff8908d42">
      <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy requires repaying missed premiums with interest, implying that cancellation through cash withdrawal is a prerequisite for such action.</data>
      <data key="d4">precondition for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c9e7b542-afe9-4463-8362-f1e619e1c1fa" target="90a0bf93-4726-45a8-be6a-15b19f92a2cc">
      <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy within two years necessitates settling unpaid premiums with added interest, making it a prerequisite for resuming coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c9e7b542-afe9-4463-8362-f1e619e1c1fa" target="2c2ac373-cacf-48f8-8261-4cacaba45a95">
      <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy requires payment of past-due premiums plus interest, which is relevant given the policy’s non-medical underwriting nature leading to a graded benefit structure.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c9e7b542-afe9-4463-8362-f1e619e1c1fa" target="1041bf2f-c9a6-4ed4-9190-43134b349c16">
      <data key="d3">Reinstating a policy requires payment of past-due premiums plus interest, but this option may not apply to individuals who exceed the maximum eligible age.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c9e7b542-afe9-4463-8362-f1e619e1c1fa" target="9740e07b-e5dc-49f2-906f-8809e5ba6736">
      <data key="d3">The possibility of restarting the policy through payment of missed premiums with interest safeguards the validity of Linda Sue Johnson’s role as beneficiary should the policy lapse.</data>
