    <edge source="6f5e1101-0f4f-4e81-8e61-d356e62a3dc6" target="e96a90d3-556d-4069-8f21-af575f151db0">
      <data key="d3">Since the policy is guaranteed issue with no medical questions, the 30-day free look period serves as an essential safeguard for consumers entering a non-underwritten contract.</data>
      <data key="d4">justified by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6f5e1101-0f4f-4e81-8e61-d356e62a3dc6" target="dc94da25-01fa-41ec-97bf-06bd13328b2f">
      <data key="d3">Because the policy is issued without medical questions, it justifies offering a 30-day free look period, allowing policyholders to assess coverage risk-free before finalizing enrollment.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6f5e1101-0f4f-4e81-8e61-d356e62a3dc6" target="10e87b42-cc43-4448-a557-8ed5882b14c8">
      <data key="d3">Since the policy requires no medical exam, it ensures accessibility for applicants who may not qualify through traditional underwriting. This absence of medical screening supports broader access, including those seeking portable coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6f5e1101-0f4f-4e81-8e61-d356e62a3dc6" target="2c2ac373-cacf-48f8-8261-4cacaba45a95">
      <data key="d3">The policy's issuance without medical questions creates an increased risk exposure for the insurer, necessitating a graded benefit schedule during the initial coverage period to limit payout amounts until certain conditions are met.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
