      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2c2ac373-cacf-48f8-8261-4cacaba45a95" target="2037f96e-c50f-40b7-a609-fab5cbf6d95c">
      <data key="d3">The presence of a graded benefit arises from the policy being guaranteed issue without medical underwriting, which allows continued coverage even after missed premiums beyond the initial term.</data>
      <data key="d4">caused by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2c2ac373-cacf-48f8-8261-4cacaba45a95" target="23ea9eda-ab01-439d-8c9f-2e04c0f63d59">
      <data key="d3">The absence of medical requirements triggers a graded benefit schedule, which results in reduced benefits if the policy continues past the second year without further payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
